---
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/LegalPage.astro";
import { business, addressFull } from "../data/business";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${business.displayName} collects, uses, and protects information from families who use this website.`}
  path="/privacy"
  effectiveDate="October 12, 2026"
  noindex
>
  <p>
    {business.legalName}, doing business as {business.displayName} ("we," "us"), runs this website. This
    policy explains what information we collect through it, why, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you give us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email, optional phone number, your message, and, if
      you are asking about a party or event, the type of event, a preferred date, your child's age,
      and an approximate guest count.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Trial class booking:</strong> the booking form on our booking page is provided by Dojo
      Forge, our class management software. It collects a parent or guardian's name, phone, and
      email, and the student's name and age, and passes them to us so we can schedule your visit.
      Dojo Forge processes that information on our behalf.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How you found us:</strong> if you send the contact form, it includes how you first
      arrived at our site (for example, the ad or link you clicked, saved in your browser on your
      first visit) and, if you choose to tell us, how you heard about us.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Phone calls and email</strong> you send us directly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children's information</h2>
  <p>
    Our programs serve children, but this website is meant for parents and guardians. We collect a
    child's name and age only when a parent or guardian provides them to book a class or plan an
    event. We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children under 13. If you
    believe a child has sent us information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> measures how visitors use the site (pages viewed, device and
      browser type, approximate location, and events such as tapping our phone number or starting a
      booking). Google may use cookies to do this.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Meta Pixel</strong> helps us measure and improve our Facebook and Instagram advertising.
      When you send our contact form, we use Meta's Advanced Matching, which sends your email, phone
      number, and name to Meta in hashed (scrambled) form so Meta can match the visit to an account.
      Meta's handling of that data is described in Meta's own privacy policy.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Maps:</strong> our contact page embeds a Google map, which lets Google set cookies
      and receive your IP address when the map loads.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this site, runs Turnstile (a spam check on our contact form), and
      delivers contact form messages to our inbox by email. Cloudflare processes technical data such
      as IP addresses to deliver and protect the site.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Analytics and advertising tools run only on our live website, not on test copies. You can limit
    them with your browser's cookie settings, an ad blocker, or the opt-out tools Google and Meta
    provide.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer your questions and schedule trial classes, parties, and events.</li>
    <li>To contact you about the visit or event you asked about.</li>
    <li>To understand how the website is used and improve it and our advertising.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with the service providers named in
    this policy (Dojo Forge, Cloudflare, Google, and Meta), only as described above, and when the law
    requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Text messages</h2>
  <p>
    We do not send text messages yet. When we start, we will text only people who have given explicit
    consent, and our <a href="/sms-terms">SMS Terms</a> will apply. Mobile numbers and text messaging
    consent are never shared with third parties or affiliates for their own marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>
    We do not keep anyone's personal information for longer than one year. If you are a prospective
    student, or the parent of one, and you tell us you are not interested in our programs, we delete
    your information sooner, once you let us know.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to see, correct, or delete the information we hold about you or your child by
    contacting us using the details below.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how we handle information, we will update this page and the effective date at the
    top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    {business.displayName}<br />
    {addressFull}<br />
    <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a> &middot; <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
